// Field classification registry — the single source of truth the Prisma
// Client Extension (config/db.js) and the historical backfill script both
// read. ALLOWLIST model: a String field absent here gets ZERO
// transformation, since 'String' in the Prisma schema also covers UUID FK
// scalars, generated PKs, and other non-text values that must never be
// touched.
//
// Generated by scripts/generate-field-rules.js, then reviewed by hand.
// Every field defaults to RULES.NONE (general normalization only — trim,
// collapse whitespace, strip invisible characters, no case change) unless
// a clear pattern justifies UPPER (business codes) / LOWER (free-typed
// system identifiers: email, username) / PHONE. Fixed-vocabulary
// dropdown-driven fields (status/type/category/role/etc.) are
// deliberately RULES.NONE, not lowercase, per explicit confirmation — this
// codebase compares many of them against UPPERCASE literals elsewhere
// (e.g. `status === 'PENDING'`), so forcing lowercase would silently break
// those comparisons.
//
// Regenerate the draft (scripts/generate-field-rules.js) whenever a new
// String field is added to the schema, then diff and merge by hand —
// never overwrite this file wholesale.

